{"key":"b4d30e1c-65a6-43a6-b0c5-526a414596b3","installationKey":"5ae8b93d-03d9-48f1-8334-f1f251d13f1f","publishingOrganizationKey":"b6d09100-919d-4026-b35b-22be3dae7156","doi":"10.15468/nztdvb","version":"1.2","external":false,"numConstituents":0,"type":"SAMPLING_EVENT","title":"Amphibian Migration Monitoring at Marsh-Billings-Rockefeller NHP in Vermont, USA (1999-2000)","description":"In order to help guide the development of a forest management plan, a biological inventory of the\namphibian and reptiles within the park and adjacent lands was conducted in 1999 and 2000. Amphibian spring migration to vernal pools were monitored using a drift fence and pitfall traps. Additionally, captures of small mammals were also recorded. Prior to the start of the 1999 amphibian breeding season, four, 30.5-meter long drift fences, each with 8 pitfall traps (consisting of two #10 cans attached end to end) buried along their length, were established at two different forested wetlands. Pitfall traps were typically opened on rainy days or when rain was\nexpected overnight, and then checked the following morning.","language":"eng","citation":{"text":"Faccio S, McFarland K (2022). Amphibian Migration Monitoring at Marsh-Billings-Rockefeller NHP in Vermont, USA (1999-2000). Version 1.2. Vermont Center for Ecostudies. Sampling event dataset https://doi.org/10.15468/nztdvb accessed via GBIF.org on 2026-10-26.","citationProvidedBySource":false},"contactsCitation":[{"key":3464873,"abbreviatedName":"Faccio S","firstName":"Steve","lastName":"Faccio","roles":["ORIGINATOR"],"userId":["http://orcid.org/0000-0001-5098-9265"]},{"key":3464874,"abbreviatedName":"McFarland K","firstName":"Kent","lastName":"McFarland","roles":["METADATA_AUTHOR"],"userId":["https://orcid.org/0000-0001-7809-5503"]}],"lockedForAutoUpdate":false,"createdBy":"b6d09100-919d-4026-b35b-22be3dae7156","modifiedBy":"jwaller","created":"2022-03-29T21:14:26.708+00:00","modified":"2025-12-17T14:50:44.209+00:00","contacts":[{"key":3